WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.899
What a working engineer takes from this.

2
00:00:02.179 --> 00:00:08.749
Use public benchmarks to build a shortlist, favoring ones that resist contamination and report the harness.

3
00:00:09.029 --> 00:00:10.352
Discount small gaps.

4
00:00:10.632 --> 00:00:19.379
Expect agents to be strongest on well-specified tasks with good tests and weakest where context is tribal and success is hard to check.

5
00:00:19.659 --> 00:00:25.227
Treat productivity claims, from vendors and skeptics alike, as hypotheses about your team.

6
00:00:25.507 --> 00:00:32.013
And measure your own work, because none of these studies used your codebase, your conventions, or your review standards.

7
00:00:32.293 --> 00:00:35.621
Lesson 3 shows how to run that measurement in an afternoon.
